    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n- **Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was being imported as a named export but wasn't exported from `src/finetune/index.js`\n- **Solution**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n**2. Evaluation test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function had signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused references to be misinterpreted as banned terms, flagging all output as toxic.\n- **Solution**: Fixed the signature to `(outputs, references = undefined, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so references are properly ignored and the default banned terms are used\n\n**Test Results**: All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2705",
